Barcode scanner (html5-qrcode)
BarcodeScannerPage.tsx:113-126 — cleanup on unmount does call stopScanner() and forcibly clears the #reader DOM node, which is good defensive coding against the known html5-qrcode "camera left running" issue. However stopScanner is async while the useEffect cleanup calls it via void stopScanner() — if the component unmounts while html5QrCodeRef.current.stop() is still pending, the ref reset (:107) happens after the async work resolves, by which time the component tree is gone; no functional bug observed but it's a fire-and-forget pattern that could race if the user navigates away and immediately back into the scanner page (isTransitioningRef guard mitigates most of this). Low
Permission-denied and no-camera errors are handled with user-friendly messages (:72-85) — good coverage.
Camera restarts automatically after handleAddToCart success (:183) but not after "Product not found" — user must manually click "Scan Again" (:318-320), which is a reasonable but inconsistent UX choice, not a bug.
