Retail ERP — Codebase Audit & MVP Roadmap

Key takeaway up front: this codebase is already a full retail ERP (POS, purchases, payments, deliveries, expenses, stock adjustments, barcode scanning, analytics) — well past a typical "MVP" feature-wise. The real gap isn't building more, it's fixing what's already there.

30 findings, most important 6 (Critical):

JWT secret falls back to a hardcoded default if the env var is unset — every token becomes forgeable
No rate limiting on login/register — open to brute force
Seed scripts create a real admin account (admin@example.com / password123) with no production guard
Zero test coverage anywhere in the repo
Stock/sale/purchase writes use Mongo transactions that require a replica set, but .env.example ships a standalone Mongo URI — will hard-fail on that config
Dashboard "Total Revenue" is computed from a different collection than actual sales revenue and the two are never reconciled — the headline number can just be wrong
Also flagged as high-severity: JWT stored in localStorage (XSS risk), no global 401 handling, and — root-causing a lot of the frontend inconsistency — the components/ and layouts/ folders are empty, so every page hand-rolls its own table/loading/error UI (which is why loading states only got fixed on 3 of ~8 pages).

The roadmap is 6 phases: stop-the-bleeding security/data fixes → lock MVP scope → fix the frontend at the root (shared components, 401 handling) → validation/data integrity → a test safety net → cleanup. Full detail, file:line citations, and effort estimates are in the artifact.